        "title": "Roman and Medieval Theater",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Roman theater adapted and transformed Greek models; medieval theater largely reinvented theatrical performance from scratch after the near-total collapse of professional theater in late antiquity. These two periods bracket the gap — what survived, what was lost, and how theatrical performance re-emerged through the Church's own rituals."
